1
00:00:00,777 --> 00:00:09,157
I found myself lost and alone on this journey

2
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:17,497
Though my heart wandered far and wide, I could move not an inch

3
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:22,587
But now I can depart for any distant land

4
00:00:22,587 --> 00:00:25,717
But now I can depart for any distant land

5
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:28,757
Now that we've met on this road

6
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:34,557
Now that we've met on this road

7
00:00:35,057 --> 00:00:42,397
Even the unfamiliar songs of travelers

8
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:53,157
Can spark nostalgia in me when I'm with you

9
00:00:53,157 --> 00:00:57,037
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

10
00:00:57,037 --> 00:01:01,417
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

11
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:09,847
Then let's go search for it beyond the wind

12
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:13,807
Through chilling dawns,

13
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:18,227
Through arid noons,

14
00:01:18,227 --> 00:01:22,187
Through shivering nights,

15
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:28,197
Let's go see what lies at the end

16
00:01:31,467 --> 00:01:36,727
You must be in the middle of a deal since you've come at a time like this.

17
00:01:36,727 --> 00:01:37,537
Need a certificate?

18
00:01:37,537 --> 00:01:38,777
Yes.

19
00:01:38,777 --> 00:01:43,947
I hope you become a merchant who'll intimidate his clientele by name alone in the near future.

20
00:01:44,637 --> 00:01:45,667
My thoughts exactly.

21
00:01:46,067 --> 00:01:50,367
Oh, by the way, would you happen to know anyone who'd like to travel to Lamtra?

22
00:01:50,367 --> 00:01:53,627
Geez, it seems like everyone here falls for the same trap.

23
00:01:53,627 --> 00:01:56,137
Dazzled by a certain young shepherdess, eh?

24
00:01:56,567 --> 00:01:58,277
No, I...

25
00:01:58,277 --> 00:02:01,217
She's the only person who wanders that area unscathed.

26
00:02:01,217 --> 00:02:05,347
I don't think I have to tell you what the Church thinks about that.

27
00:02:05,347 --> 00:02:09,537
Don't involve yourself with her if you don't want to find yourself in a mess.

28
00:02:10,227 --> 00:02:15,317
Norah the Fairy does seem to be your type of girl, though.

29
00:02:15,317 --> 00:02:17,317
G-Give me a break.

30
00:02:18,547 --> 00:02:22,027
Who do I make the certificate out to? Or should I leave it blank?

31
00:02:22,027 --> 00:02:24,577
Make it out to Lemerio Trading, please

32
00:02:26,197 --> 00:02:30,837
You already have a buyer... Did you purchase on credit or something?

33
00:02:30,837 --> 00:02:32,927
Yes. Is that a bad thing?

34
00:02:32,927 --> 00:02:35,677
Oh, you'll find out soon enough.

35
00:02:36,407 --> 00:02:38,597
Did any major price fluctuations occur?

36
00:02:38,927 --> 00:02:41,127
No, there's no reason to worry too much.

37
00:02:41,127 --> 00:02:44,357
I'm sure you of all people will be able to turn it to your advantage.

38
00:02:45,737 --> 00:02:49,977
Oh, and wait a bit before letting any pretty girls ensnare you, y'hear?

39
00:02:49,977 --> 00:02:52,477
They'll soak up all your profits just like that!

40
00:02:52,827 --> 00:02:55,357
I wouldn't invest if I didn't anticipate returns.

41
00:02:55,357 --> 00:02:57,357
Hahaha! Is that so?

42
00:02:57,747 --> 00:02:59,747
Here's the certificate.

43
00:02:59,747 --> 00:03:01,047
Thank you very much.

44
00:03:02,257 --> 00:03:04,067
Please wish me lots of luck.

45
00:03:04,697 --> 00:03:09,707
Wolf and Conspiracies

46
00:03:10,047 --> 00:03:11,707
Sorry to keep you waiting, Holo.

47
00:03:15,067 --> 00:03:18,527
They were precious. Called me a pretty little snowdrop, they did.

48
00:03:18,527 --> 00:03:23,087
They're no different from hungry dogs. Don't bother with them or they might take you away.

49
00:03:23,087 --> 00:03:26,647
If I'm kidnapped, you'll just have to rescue me again.

50
00:03:26,637 --> 00:03:27,657
Am I wrong?

51
00:03:27,657 --> 00:03:29,327
Sure, I'd rescue you.

52
00:03:29,327 --> 00:03:33,277
Of course, in the end, I was the one who rescued you.

53
00:03:34,507 --> 00:03:39,277
Well, I don't know what kind of return you're expecting,

54
00:03:40,147 --> 00:03:42,777
but go ahead and invest to your heart's content.

55
00:03:43,637 --> 00:03:44,937
You heard all that?

56
00:03:45,887 --> 00:03:48,457
I didn't know you liked blondes.

57
00:03:49,077 --> 00:03:54,227
Are you attracted to her scrawny appearance? Or do you like the way her cares are etched on her face?

58
00:03:54,227 --> 00:03:56,337
Or do you just have a thing for shepherdesses?

59
00:03:56,337 --> 00:04:00,967
Wait a second! He and I were just shooting the breeze. I'm not—

60
00:04:02,007 --> 00:04:02,927
You're not what?

61
00:04:04,447 --> 00:04:07,517
W-Well, sure, I thought Norah was nice.

62
00:04:07,517 --> 00:04:10,477
I can't say our conversation wasn't fun.

63
00:04:10,477 --> 00:04:16,897
But that doesn't mean I don't care about you, or—well, it doesn't mean that!

64
00:04:18,727 --> 00:04:22,497
Well... I was just trying to tease you a little...

65
00:04:23,987 --> 00:04:25,497
But...

66
00:04:27,827 --> 00:04:30,287
I didn't expect you to take it so seriously.

67
00:04:31,347 --> 00:04:33,907
I'm happy.

68
00:04:35,427 --> 00:04:36,477
Holo...

69
00:04:37,147 --> 00:04:38,127
However,

70
00:04:39,057 --> 00:04:42,007
males simply say whatever's convenient.

71
00:04:46,207 --> 00:04:47,887
I'm a merchant.

72
00:04:47,887 --> 00:04:50,057
I'm a man of my word.

73
00:04:50,847 --> 00:04:56,057
I know that knights entrust their shields and swords as proof of sincerity.

74
00:04:56,517 --> 00:04:59,017
What can you entrust to me as a merchant?

75
00:04:59,867 --> 00:05:02,957
Very well. I'll prove my sincerity to you.

76
00:05:03,567 --> 00:05:05,787
I'll buy you peaches preserved in honey—

77
00:05:08,257 --> 00:05:11,077
Hmm? What will you buy me?

78
00:05:11,077 --> 00:05:14,327
You can't do that! You're crossing the line!

79
00:05:14,327 --> 00:05:17,287
You said I should ask more charmingly.

80
00:05:17,287 --> 00:05:19,627
I said you should ask nicely!

81
00:05:19,627 --> 00:05:21,337
Not to use your feminine wiles!

82
00:05:21,337 --> 00:05:23,317
Didn't you think I was cute, though?

83
00:05:26,177 --> 00:05:31,087
My heart was racing more from your reaction than from worrying about whether my scheme would work.

84
00:05:33,377 --> 00:05:35,847
Come on, now. Don't be so upset.

85
00:05:35,847 --> 00:05:37,697
I was happy to hear you say that, truly.

86
00:05:38,377 --> 00:05:40,107
Are you angry all the same?

87
00:05:43,857 --> 00:05:47,237
All right. I'm not upset, okay? I'm not upset.

88
00:05:47,237 --> 00:05:48,447
Are you satisfied?

89
00:05:49,907 --> 00:05:51,527
It won't do to get separated.

90
00:05:51,527 --> 00:05:54,007
May I take your hand?

91
00:05:55,917 --> 00:05:57,997
Yeah, losing sight of you would cause problems.

92
00:06:00,377 --> 00:06:03,007
In any case, business is scary.

93
00:06:04,137 --> 00:06:07,217
You need to use your head in order to make money,

94
00:06:07,217 --> 00:06:09,587
but if you go too far and your plans fail,

95
00:06:09,587 --> 00:06:14,637
you'll end up like Latparon Trading and be forced to sell goods at half the price.

96
00:06:16,307 --> 00:06:17,947
But if you do it right,

97
00:06:17,947 --> 00:06:21,777
you could make huge profits with something simple, like moving armor on margin.

98
00:06:22,307 --> 00:06:24,187
That's the essence of business.

99
00:06:24,187 --> 00:06:29,367
But the fact that you're in debt doesn't sit well with me, even if it is temporary.

100
00:06:30,247 --> 00:06:31,817
Are you talking about buying on credit?

101
00:06:31,817 --> 00:06:32,987
That's right.

102
00:06:32,987 --> 00:06:38,997
You bought a hundred Lumione worth of armor at half price, which means you're in debt to Latparon, right?

103
00:06:38,997 --> 00:06:46,347
Yeah, I'll sell them to Lemerio Trading at market price, and
my debt will be settled between the two trading companies.

104
00:06:46,827 --> 00:06:51,017
I'm dealing with double my net worth, so the profit I make will be double what it would normally be.

105
00:06:52,507 --> 00:06:55,647
Isn't it worth the worry even if you're not fond of the idea?

106
00:06:57,267 --> 00:06:58,977
Well, you might be right.

107
00:07:17,427 --> 00:07:20,287
Is this place run by a friar?

108
00:07:21,537 --> 00:07:24,627
We'd be hearing the sound of prayers if that were the case.

109
00:07:27,917 --> 00:07:32,007
I bet you can't hear a thing over the sound of chewing my meat pie.

110
00:07:32,007 --> 00:07:34,117
You have a fine sense of wry humor,

111
00:07:34,117 --> 00:07:38,557
but for the sake of my reputation, I'll tell you that I can hear the sound of someone in the building.

112
00:07:38,987 --> 00:07:40,097
There are people inside?

113
00:07:40,097 --> 00:07:45,357
Indeed. But the atmosphere's unpleasant,
and it's definitely not lively in there.

114
00:07:46,237 --> 00:07:47,857
Hesitating won't get me anywhere...

115
00:07:48,307 --> 00:07:50,857
We can't make money if we don't sell the goods.

116
00:07:51,267 --> 00:07:53,987
And a meat pie's no good unless you eat it.

117
00:07:54,907 --> 00:07:57,287
I was saving that, you know.

118
00:07:57,287 --> 00:07:59,867
Oh? If you wanted some, you should have asked.

119
00:07:59,877 --> 00:08:00,827
Here.

120
00:08:08,177 --> 00:08:10,637
There's still some time left before the sabbath.

121
00:08:10,637 --> 00:08:12,637
Did something unusual happen?

122
00:08:13,237 --> 00:08:15,507
Well, something like that.

123
00:08:15,927 --> 00:08:18,017
Did you just arrive today, sir?

124
00:08:18,477 --> 00:08:22,267
No, I came here a few days ago.
You know how it goes.

125
00:08:22,727 --> 00:08:26,477
I can see that you're rather popular, sir.

126
00:08:26,477 --> 00:08:27,737
Not at all.

127
00:08:28,187 --> 00:08:29,937
Well, excuse me.

128
00:08:29,937 --> 00:08:31,237
I see.

129
00:08:31,737 --> 00:08:34,237
I look forward to seeing you again,

130
00:08:35,487 --> 00:08:36,697
Craft Lawrence-san.

131
00:08:39,947 --> 00:08:41,577
It's as I thought.

132
00:08:42,077 --> 00:08:45,547
I see that you've brought armor from Latparon Trading with you.

133
00:08:45,547 --> 00:08:46,637
How did you know?

134
00:08:46,637 --> 00:08:49,417
Actually, we were notified by a messenger on horseback.

135
00:08:49,417 --> 00:08:53,837
Latparon Trading assigned the debt to us.

136
00:08:53,837 --> 00:08:55,217
They transferred the debt?!

137
00:08:58,227 --> 00:09:00,007
What's going on?

138
00:09:00,007 --> 00:09:02,977
Your companion has failed miserably at business.

139
00:09:03,347 --> 00:09:04,977
Just as we have.

140
00:09:05,517 --> 00:09:06,847
What?

141
00:09:06,847 --> 00:09:11,107
The armor market crashed a while ago, and it's worth almost nothing now.

142
00:09:11,107 --> 00:09:17,097
Latparon let him borrow money towards worthless stock and transferred the rights to our company.

143
00:09:17,097 --> 00:09:20,867
Long story short, your companion was left with only his monstrous debt.

144
00:09:20,867 --> 00:09:23,207
In other words, he's bankrupt.

145
00:09:25,657 --> 00:09:26,707
You've...

146
00:09:28,127 --> 00:09:29,537
I was tricked...

147
00:09:33,377 --> 00:09:36,677
We both live by such agreements.

148
00:09:36,677 --> 00:09:38,047
I'm sure you understand.

149
00:09:38,387 --> 00:09:42,057
Of course, Lemerio-san. I'm a merchant, after all.

150
00:09:42,057 --> 00:09:47,517
Lawrence-san, you purchased one hundred Lumione worth of arms from Latparon Trading.

151
00:09:47,517 --> 00:09:53,607
Out of that, forty-seven and three-fourths Lumione was financed with debt—and a due date.

152
00:09:53,607 --> 00:09:56,567
I request immediate payment of your financial obligations.

153
00:09:56,577 --> 00:10:01,577
We will have to ask the Lohen Trading Union to assume your debt if you cannot pay.

154
00:10:02,487 --> 00:10:03,197
Understood.

155
00:10:03,197 --> 00:10:07,997
Well, the deadline for payment is the day after tomorrow, so we'll wait two days

156
00:10:07,997 --> 00:10:13,717
for you to return the forty-seven and 3/4 Lumione.

157
00:10:14,457 --> 00:10:17,377
I'll find a way to sell the armor for a high price.

158
00:10:17,377 --> 00:10:20,347
We'll settle the balance in two days. Will that do?

159
00:10:20,797 --> 00:10:21,717
Yes.

160
00:10:22,387 --> 00:10:23,797
Well then, I'll get going.

161
00:10:25,517 --> 00:10:27,937
Just to let you know,

162
00:10:27,937 --> 00:10:33,567
we do have open air vendors at every town gate that can certainly fulfill any of your needs.

163
00:10:33,567 --> 00:10:36,947
Please do not hesitate to make use of them.

164
00:10:37,357 --> 00:10:40,697
I appreciate the offer, but I think I'll respectfully decline

165
00:10:41,117 --> 00:10:43,697
since you'll probably be busy enough with other customers.

166
00:10:44,487 --> 00:10:47,077
I look forward to seeing you in two days.

167
00:10:47,077 --> 00:10:49,627
May God be with you.

168
00:10:55,677 --> 00:10:57,417
Sorry to keep you waiting.

169
00:10:59,597 --> 00:11:01,927
So...

170
00:11:03,047 --> 00:11:05,347
Explain what happened in there.

171
00:11:05,717 --> 00:11:09,887
Basically, the merchandise we're carrying has turned into scrap.

172
00:11:09,887 --> 00:11:12,857
Then I suppose I didn't hear wrong.

173
00:11:12,857 --> 00:11:15,857
This could mean bankruptcy for me.

174
00:11:19,697 --> 00:11:20,867
Should we run?

175
00:11:22,777 --> 00:11:25,867
The information networks among merchants are like the eyes of God.

176
00:11:26,577 --> 00:11:29,707
If I tried to do business anywhere, I'd be found out immediately.

177
00:11:29,707 --> 00:11:32,747
I'd never be able to work as a merchant again.

178
00:11:32,747 --> 00:11:36,917
But wounded animals are eaten to the bone.

179
00:11:37,417 --> 00:11:38,917
Will you accept that fate?

180
00:11:39,377 --> 00:11:41,217
Who said I'd do that?

181
00:11:41,217 --> 00:11:44,927
I just need to return forty-seven Lumione gold coins.

182
00:11:45,217 --> 00:11:47,337
It shouldn't be too difficult to make ends meet.

183
00:11:49,057 --> 00:11:51,307
I'm Holo, the wise wolf.

184
00:11:51,307 --> 00:11:53,307
I'll certainly help in any way I can.

185
00:11:53,307 --> 00:11:57,647
You could help me a great deal by cutting back on the amount you eat every—

186
00:11:58,897 --> 00:12:00,657
I said all along I'd pay for my own food.

187
00:12:01,397 --> 00:12:02,817
I was kidding.

188
00:12:03,657 --> 00:12:04,867
If you can joke, you'll be fine.

189
00:12:04,867 --> 00:12:08,367
If worse comes to worst, upon my honor, I will help you escape...

190
00:12:08,907 --> 00:12:11,287
even if I must use the power within the wheat.

191
00:12:11,297 --> 00:12:15,537
You promised to take me to the northern woods.

192
00:12:15,537 --> 00:12:17,887
I can't have you getting tripped up here.

193
00:12:18,957 --> 00:12:22,197
I'll keep that promise, and...

194
00:12:25,167 --> 00:12:28,717
If it comes to it, I may need saving.

195
00:12:28,717 --> 00:12:30,977
Okay. Count on it.

196
00:12:30,977 --> 00:12:33,477
I'll stop by the trading house for now.

197
00:12:33,477 --> 00:12:34,607
Wait for me at the inn—

198
00:12:36,397 --> 00:12:42,817
Do I look like the kind of ungrateful wolf that would groom her tail and let her companion face a crisis alone?

199
00:12:42,817 --> 00:12:44,597
No, but...

200
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:46,067
Do I look like that kind of wolf?

201
00:12:46,067 --> 00:12:47,697
No, you don't.

202
00:12:47,697 --> 00:12:49,627
But that's not the point.

203
00:12:49,617 --> 00:12:51,997
Then what <i>is</i> the point?

204
00:12:53,907 --> 00:12:56,247
The trading house is like home for us merchants.

205
00:12:57,127 --> 00:13:00,167
You understand what bringing a girl home means, right?

206
00:13:00,667 --> 00:13:03,127
Why can't you simply explain the situation?

207
00:13:03,127 --> 00:13:04,967
How do you expect me to do that?

208
00:13:04,967 --> 00:13:07,637
I wouldn't know what to do if they reported you to the Church.

209
00:13:08,757 --> 00:13:12,057
In that case, just tell them we're lovers or something!

210
00:13:16,967 --> 00:13:18,147
All right.

211
00:13:18,147 --> 00:13:19,107
You can come with me.

212
00:13:19,857 --> 00:13:22,647
You're more quick-witted than I am anyway.

213
00:13:22,647 --> 00:13:24,607
Indeed. Leave it to me.

214
00:13:24,607 --> 00:13:27,487
But I'll tell them that you're a business associate.

215
00:13:27,487 --> 00:13:29,197
You don't need to say anything beyond that.

216
00:13:29,197 --> 00:13:29,867
Okay.

217
00:13:29,877 --> 00:13:32,627
That bunch can give a rough welcome.

218
00:13:33,157 --> 00:13:34,967
Don't you worry about me.

219
00:13:35,657 --> 00:13:40,587
First off, I want to know who this lovely lady might be.

220
00:13:41,047 --> 00:13:43,587
She's a business partner. We're traveling together.

221
00:13:44,467 --> 00:13:45,587
Business?

222
00:13:47,047 --> 00:13:51,847
She single-handedly increased the value of my marten furs

223
00:13:51,847 --> 00:13:55,057
from 140 to 210 Trenni coins at the Milone Trading in Pazzio.

224
00:13:55,057 --> 00:13:56,097
What?

225
00:13:56,097 --> 00:13:59,607
I did say this morning that I'd see a return from investing in her.

226
00:14:01,357 --> 00:14:03,607
Pairs like you show up ever so often.

227
00:14:04,527 --> 00:14:05,987
Well, whatever.

228
00:14:05,987 --> 00:14:10,867
The scriptures say not to carelessly open a mysterious box.

229
00:14:10,877 --> 00:14:11,987
A wise decision.

230
00:14:16,997 --> 00:14:18,117
Well...

231
00:14:19,167 --> 00:14:22,247
Let's move on to the main topic.

232
00:14:22,247 --> 00:14:27,637
A man from Lemerio Trading just came to talk to us about
assuming your debt, so I have a general idea of what's going on.

233
00:14:28,087 --> 00:14:32,007
In short, you got greedy and had the rug pulled out from under you, correct?

234
00:14:32,007 --> 00:14:32,927
Yes.

235
00:14:32,927 --> 00:14:34,637
That makes things rather simple.

236
00:14:35,717 --> 00:14:42,397
You yourself must pay back the debt that this guild, in all likelihood, will be faced with.

237
00:14:42,897 --> 00:14:48,447
If you were swindled, robbed, or suffered losses due to illness or injury,

238
00:14:48,447 --> 00:14:52,407
then upon our honor, we would have helped you. But not this time.

239
00:14:52,417 --> 00:14:56,157
The only one who can save you is God—or this beauty.

240
00:14:56,697 --> 00:14:58,077
I'm fully aware of that.

241
00:14:58,077 --> 00:15:01,667
Unfortunately, I'm not in a position where I can show you any compassion.

242
00:15:01,667 --> 00:15:06,337
It's because I know the need to be strict at times like this that I get to stay in that gathering hall.

243
00:15:06,337 --> 00:15:08,667
The Union's laws bind us all.

244
00:15:09,217 --> 00:15:10,547
Of course.

245
00:15:10,547 --> 00:15:14,847
I'd be as upset as anyone if a member were treated as an exception to the rule.

246
00:15:14,847 --> 00:15:17,517
Loans among Union members aren't allowed, either.

247
00:15:17,887 --> 00:15:19,017
I'm aware of that.

248
00:15:19,017 --> 00:15:21,517
Your obligation comes due in two days, correct?

249
00:15:21,517 --> 00:15:24,897
Lemerio is burdened by their own failed armor investments.

250
00:15:24,897 --> 00:15:27,397
They won't hesitate to demand payment.

251
00:15:27,897 --> 00:15:33,737
In other words, your failure will be made public the day after tomorrow, and I'll have to detain you.

252
00:15:33,737 --> 00:15:36,407
What do you think will happen at that time?

253
00:15:36,867 --> 00:15:42,497
There won't be a future for me unless I come up with forty-seven Lumione within two days.

254
00:15:42,497 --> 00:15:45,167
It's not that you won't have a future.

255
00:15:45,167 --> 00:15:47,587
There will be a fate that awaits you.

256
00:15:47,587 --> 00:15:53,047
But it will be one that is black, bitter, and heavy.

257
00:15:54,137 --> 00:15:59,387
You could pay back a debt of forty-seven Lumione in ten years by rowing a long-distance ship.

258
00:15:59,387 --> 00:16:01,477
You could also work in a mine.

259
00:16:01,477 --> 00:16:03,967
If you're lucky enough to survive that long, of course.

260
00:16:05,177 --> 00:16:06,687
A nightmare come to life.

261
00:16:06,697 --> 00:16:08,777
Don't forget, though.

262
00:16:08,777 --> 00:16:11,697
It's not that I want to see you die.

263
00:16:11,697 --> 00:16:16,447
Sins must be punished. It's my duty to enforce that simple principle.

264
00:16:16,987 --> 00:16:18,117
I understand.

265
00:16:21,157 --> 00:16:23,627
Do what you can in the next two days.

266
00:16:23,997 --> 00:16:26,837
If you need my help with business, I'll do whatever I can.

267
00:16:26,837 --> 00:16:29,087
I have faith in you.

268
00:16:29,087 --> 00:16:32,047
Go out there and give it your best shot.

269
00:16:33,257 --> 00:16:35,137
I appreciate your concern.

270
00:16:35,717 --> 00:16:38,557
I'll find a way to manage in two days, somehow.

271
00:16:38,557 --> 00:16:45,107
There are always possibilities in business—and some you can only see when you are in true danger.

272
00:16:51,257 --> 00:16:55,447
Is there anything else you'd like to say or ask?

273
00:16:55,447 --> 00:16:56,367
No.

274
00:16:56,987 --> 00:16:57,797
Excuse us.

275
00:17:03,327 --> 00:17:04,207
There is one thing.

276
00:17:05,207 --> 00:17:09,297
You should start thinking about what to say when I repay my debts.

277
00:17:13,797 --> 00:17:15,837
If you can still talk like that, you'll be fine.

278
00:17:16,147 --> 00:17:17,757
I'll see you soon.

279
00:17:18,927 --> 00:17:21,847
Forty-seven Lumione in two days, huh?

280
00:17:35,527 --> 00:17:38,027
What are you going to do?

281
00:17:38,027 --> 00:17:40,287
I'll divide the debt into smaller debts for the time being.

282
00:17:40,587 --> 00:17:42,447
Do you have people you can borrow from?

283
00:17:42,447 --> 00:17:44,917
I'm a businessman, you know.

284
00:17:45,577 --> 00:17:51,567
I don't know anyone who'll lend me a substantial amount of money, but I do know a lot of people I could ask.

285
00:17:52,457 --> 00:17:55,177
It'll be easy if you can find forty-seven people.

286
00:17:55,757 --> 00:17:57,627
Exactly.

287
00:17:57,627 --> 00:18:00,597
Oh, Lawrence-san. Long time no see!

288
00:18:00,597 --> 00:18:02,347
Have you brought me talk of profit?

289
00:18:02,847 --> 00:18:04,267
Well, to tell you the truth...

290
00:18:13,277 --> 00:18:16,067
I've barely started. There are still plenty of people I can ask.

291
00:18:17,657 --> 00:18:20,777
Unfortunately, I'm stretched pretty thin at the moment.

292
00:18:20,787 --> 00:18:24,157
Prices for wheat and meat will increase as we head into the new year.

293
00:18:28,207 --> 00:18:29,257
How did things go?

294
00:18:30,627 --> 00:18:32,117
There's always the next one.

295
00:18:33,207 --> 00:18:34,227
That's right.

296
00:18:35,007 --> 00:18:38,507
I have to stock items for the upcoming spring.

297
00:18:38,507 --> 00:18:40,507
Sorry, but I can't.

298
00:19:03,737 --> 00:19:04,697
How about we...

299
00:19:06,907 --> 00:19:10,867
Damn! Why? Why did I make that deal?

300
00:19:10,867 --> 00:19:12,537
You idiot!

301
00:19:12,537 --> 00:19:13,877
Are you...

302
00:19:15,247 --> 00:19:16,417
It's nothing.

303
00:19:17,047 --> 00:19:17,967
On to the next one.

304
00:19:49,707 --> 00:19:53,287
What about there? No, that's pointless.

305
00:19:49,907 --> 00:19:53,287
Wait. Hold on!

306
00:19:54,127 --> 00:19:55,337
What is it?

307
00:19:56,957 --> 00:20:00,797
Sorry, but I can't walk as fast as I'd like to in this form.

308
00:20:02,717 --> 00:20:04,257
No, it's my fault.

309
00:20:05,007 --> 00:20:07,017
It's been a while, Lawrence-san.

310
00:20:07,017 --> 00:20:08,847
Likewise.

311
00:20:08,847 --> 00:20:11,347
I apologize for coming after the market has closed.

312
00:20:11,347 --> 00:20:13,187
I'd like to ask you for a favor.

313
00:20:13,187 --> 00:20:15,727
I heard you've been making requests all over.

314
00:20:16,187 --> 00:20:17,937
Is it because the armor market has crashed?

315
00:20:18,777 --> 00:20:19,817
Yes.

316
00:20:19,817 --> 00:20:22,447
I made a mistake due to my lack of foresight.

317
00:20:22,457 --> 00:20:26,077
Lack of foresight? That might be.

318
00:20:26,077 --> 00:20:30,457
God is the only one who can predict the prices of commodities, though.

319
00:20:30,867 --> 00:20:33,707
It'd be cruel to criticize someone on that alone.

320
00:20:34,207 --> 00:20:37,667
Lawrence-san, I've had many opportunities to make money thanks to you.

321
00:20:37,667 --> 00:20:41,507
I've thought about helping you out if there was ever a time you were in need.

322
00:20:41,507 --> 00:20:42,127
Then...

323
00:20:42,127 --> 00:20:48,917
But you don't seem like a man who diligently lives according
to the teachings of God or is earnestly seeking relief.

324
00:20:49,967 --> 00:20:51,477
U-Um...

325
00:20:51,847 --> 00:20:53,317
What do you mean by that?

326
00:20:55,607 --> 00:21:01,787
You have the audacity to come with a girl in tow at a time you're desperately relying on people's goodwill?

327
00:21:14,787 --> 00:21:18,707
You idiot! Don't just wander into the middle of the street!

328
00:21:19,037 --> 00:21:22,007
Why... Why is this happening to me?

329
00:21:22,007 --> 00:21:22,587
Why?

330
00:21:23,167 --> 00:21:25,547
Hey! Are you okay?

331
00:21:26,217 --> 00:21:27,217
You're so pale!

332
00:21:27,637 --> 00:21:29,057
Let's go back to the inn and—

333
00:21:29,937 --> 00:21:31,467
If it wasn't for you...

334
00:21:42,717 --> 00:21:44,057
Sorry.

335
00:21:50,837 --> 00:21:52,587
I'm going back first.

336
00:23:40,677 --> 00:23:45,007
<i>Next Episode, "Wolf and the Grand Scheme."</i>

337
00:23:43,977 --> 00:23:45,977


338
00:23:45,827 --> 00:23:49,997
<i>Next Episode, "Wolf and the Grand Scheme."</i>

